  "saferAlternatives": [
    "Direct mode is read-only unless HA_ALLOW_WRITE=true; leave it unset to only inspect state, history, logs and automations. Brokered mode defaults writes on and the VomeHome key's scopes decide, so issue a key without write scopes.",
    "Use HA_DENY_DOMAINS (for example lock, alarm_control_panel, cover) or HA_ALLOW_DOMAINS to fence ha_call_service away from doors, alarms and garage openers.",
    "In direct mode config editing also needs HA_ALLOW_CONFIG_WRITE=true; keep it off and use ha_check_config and ha_render_template to test changes before applying them. In brokered mode, withhold config-write scopes from the key.",
    "Use esphome_validate and esphome_compile before esphome_upload; flashing replaces a device's firmware over the air.",
    "Prefer read tools (ha_get_state, ha_get_history, ha_get_system_log, ha_list_automations) for diagnosis; they stay on Guard's usual handling."
  ]
